    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "24c2fc89454f58e228f1125bc492ac03e032c922c05058540af6e2fecdcc0d55",
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to Paraty (about 4 hours). After a short rest, a guided jeep tour into the nature around Paraty, near the Serra da Bocaina National Park: easy trails through the Atlantic Forest lead to the crystal-clear Pedra Branca, Poço do Tarzan and Tobogã waterfalls. Visit a traditional still to learn how Paraty’s famous artisanal cachaça has been made since the 18th century, with a tasting of liqueurs and aged cachaças, and the Ouro Branco flour house, to discover the artisanal making of cassava flour, with an afternoon coffee and rapadura, a typical Brazilian sweet.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1uYRboHNcRXT7cdBOvgHyqLOB5CO0dFLj",
        "documentSha256": "5ca44e0917619e6cfc4f145271ad5de41ee5b340f983d88a219d4dc3adf3aca4",
        "paragraphs": [
